__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
tools/ui-smoke/pwenv/
frontend-v2/node_modules/
# raggity's index directory. `raggity serve`/`ingest` creates it in the CWD when
# no config points elsewhere, so running the RAG sidecar from a checkout drops a
# LanceDB index here. It is derived data — never source.
.raggity/

# Internal working notes — never published, and no longer tracked. Everything
# under `docs/` is a working note: the run-3 audit findings, the owner decisions,
# the program backlog, the design specs. They stay on the author's machine.
#
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/` so the one shipped guide can be re-included below:
# a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY cannot be re-included, no matter what the
# negation says.
docs/*
# The agent-integration guide is user-facing documentation, not a working note —
# it is shipped in the wheel/repo and pointed at from the legacy UI
# (`src/rigma/data/ui/panels.js` says "see docs/AGENTS.md"), so removing it would
# ship a dead pointer. It is the one document under `docs/` that is not internal.
!docs/AGENTS.md

# The audit findings and the research reports were published once and are now
# untracked. The code still cites them by name for provenance (55 comments point
# at a findings file, a design spec or a log excerpt), which is why the reason
# survives in the comment even though the document does not.
#
# `_research/sources/` was already excluded and stays so: it is ~5.7 MB of OTHER
# PEOPLE'S source downloaded to re-check a finding against the exact revision it
# cites — not ours to redistribute, and reproducible from the URLs the reports
# carry.
.scratch/
_research/
